<section id="process"><div class="wrap">
<h2>How a project runs</h2>
<p class="intro">Three stages, each with a sign-off before the next begins.</p>
<ol class="steps">
<li><h3>Visit and brief</h3><p>We measure the space, listen to how you use it and agree a budget.</p></li>
<li><h3>Design and approve</h3><p>You review layouts, materials and a fixed quote. Nothing starts until you say yes.</p></li>
<li><h3>Build and hand over</h3><p>Our team fits everything out and walks you through the finished space.</p></li>
</ol>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<blockquote>“They finished our office a week early and under the quote. The team now actually likes coming in.”<cite>Anita R., founder of a design-tech studio</cite></blockquote>
</div></section>

<section id="faq"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Common questions</h2>
<p class="intro"></p>
<details><summary>How long does a room makeover take?</summary><p>Most single rooms take four to six weeks from approved design to handover.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I use my existing furniture?</summary><p>Yes. We plan around pieces you want to keep and only suggest replacing what doesn’t fit.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if the final cost goes up?</summary><p>The quote you approve is fixed. Changes you request later are priced and agreed in writing first.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you work outside the city?</summary><p>We take projects within a 150 km radius. Mention your location in the form and we’ll confirm.</p></details>
</div></section>
